  "facets": [
    {
      "title": "How it works",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Other conversion paths validate base but otherwise ignore it; supplying an unsupported radix does not become harmless merely because that conversion does not use base. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/convert.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:cf701055d8c1c0f33176307c8281da439eb8227d6316510916a7c787461d571d",
          "validationStatus": "NOT-SAMPLED",
          "evidenceIds": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Conversion failures return onError when supplied; otherwise they abort the operation. Null or missing input uses onNull, defaulting to null. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/convert.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:d833c60f91df0526a40780bab1fa66c1c47ee3c9b9c6f67db3bc966a4a4ebe88",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
