          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Measurements and reference values",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "For string-to-int, long, double, or decimal conversion with an explicit base, use valid digits without prefixes such as 0x. For example, \"1010\" at base 2 becomes 10; \"A\" at base 16 becomes 10. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/convert.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:ec1cb66bc157ab48ca3952de49013e41b3f1ce5f89ce1a40d2c176efae182da0",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:32e807d7a5f377a00495a631565a3846d4fea6eab9e4518a824a9e6511702427",
            "ev:3dddd5c07486ba97851a6aa7acf88fce24eb0c6b0efd0421700b545c67b0ddfe",
            "ev:a8113206f377c09d378ec79b44c9f4e2e390cad06b05d0e6da6ea775272adcc4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "String inputs must use valid digits and fit the target numeric range; a hexadecimal 0x prefix is rejected even with base 16. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/convert.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:c81a0164b807834d62d5486c9881cd93aad9d2cd1d690d60e87752936805c0ce",
