    {
      "title": "Problems, failure modes and limitations",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "For numeric-to-string conversion, base selects the output representation: 10 becomes \"1010\" at base 2 and \"A\" at base 16. Fractional numeric inputs cause conversion failure when base is specified, including base 10. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/convert.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:ed81a6dc7e6f284e7b75d28b5ced28f5bf66b29342388107fd8af34365ff26e6",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:aa062258fa1ec7c22bc434668cb572048a4448e413f4fddc45bf769bb17e67a9"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In MongoDB 8.3.0, any explicit base, including 10, parses strings through signed long long before casting to the target. Fractional strings and values beyond signed 64-bit range therefore fail even for double or decimal targets. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/r8.3.0/src/mongo/db/exec/expression/evaluate_math.cpp",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:0a22ef41cdc87162363a0ce56cf953fc2370275db0101bed4b2a62984f6bfc39",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:a8113206f377c09d378ec79b44c9f4e2e390cad06b05d0e6da6ea775272adcc4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A Stack Overflow question reports that $toInt on the hexadecimal string \"0x0\" returns an illegal-hexadecimal-input error. This statement records the question author's reported behavior, not a test of a current server release. (low confidence)",
