    {
      "title": "Facts and statements",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "MongoDB 8.3 adds an optional $convert base expression for string/numeric conversion. Supported radices are 2, 8, 10, and 16; null behaves like omission. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/convert.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:e5b215d3aa6a86e580b6e328139a0eefe02681537f7489fdf42837b7e2d84df7",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:3dddd5c07486ba97851a6aa7acf88fce24eb0c6b0efd0421700b545c67b0ddfe",
            "ev:f38953d2dabaeba2ee5e0f567ad287376ba5c53cc8a25e5d9e4fbb0151dab9bc"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In MongoDB 8.3.0, parseBase raises 3501300 for a non-integral argument and 3501301 for an unsupported radix. Validation occurs before the ConversionFailure handler, so onError does not catch these errors. Null input returns before parseBase. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/r8.3.0/src/mongo/db/exec/expression/evaluate_math.cpp",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:e39d23747e82260292b4b20b226133e0bc64cf06eefca8f4e29ce121d162bb0c",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:3e8e1ab9fbb12341845914fd098d31f77a8f4df5c1f1253db9036bd470486be1",
            "ev:585df6beea8a67faa31b377f2db3e4eb14b7107ab75c5d7255d6fc84ed11e4a2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "NoSQLBooster 11.1 announces aggregation-helper support for MongoDB 8.3 and documents the new $convert base parameter and its four radices. This is first-party evidence of client-tool support, not independent server implementation verification. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-09-30)",
          "source": "https://www.nosqlbooster.com/blog/announcing-nosqlbooster-11-1/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:1546782f48c01018c8665a0a21f3708b47654dc42c5cd891a749eadd96839631",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:2c136c3e46c0dce4470dd8553ba746b707980d0b118739525f76454377100c78",
            "ev:89ebc087a73ae964d5ddd8f0a32a4eebf0cd542e7f62f7ed634411988255928b"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "base applies between strings and int, long, double, or decimal. Null or omitted base preserves default behavior; other conversions validate base but ignore it. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/convert.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:ab4db8ebf1f793d5f5f2b998b02d6a1f0dda94266c5e9cf9c1b5c287864dedc5",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:3dddd5c07486ba97851a6aa7acf88fce24eb0c6b0efd0421700b545c67b0ddfe",
            "ev:3e8e1ab9fbb12341845914fd098d31f77a8f4df5c1f1253db9036bd470486be1",
            "ev:585df6beea8a67faa31b377f2db3e4eb14b7107ab75c5d7255d6fc84ed11e4a2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For example, input \"1010\", to \"int\", base 2 produces 10; input 10, to \"string\", base 16 produces \"A\". (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/convert.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:6cbab178117bd13f0b39a0ef700af10c647889dfcae03d778b7d9de2eb6f0ec9",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:298205c83a7c1ae0efe0037075681f2da453f8e55945e16deb4b563b1ea54133",
            "ev:a8113206f377c09d378ec79b44c9f4e2e390cad06b05d0e6da6ea775272adcc4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "With explicit base, numeric-to-string conversion requires an integer value; 10.5 with base 2 fails or returns onError. MongoDB 8.3.0 also requires double and decimal values to fit signed long long. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/convert.md",
          "note": null,
