          "text": "An answer to the hexadecimal-conversion question defines a custom baseToDecimal expression that maps hexadecimal digits to positions in 0123456789ABCDEF, multiplies them by powers of the radix, and sums the terms. Its example converts \"A3F\" using base 16. (low confidence)",
